cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived version you used."
title: "Facety: Accountable Human Identification Protocol and Research Simulator"
type: software
version: "0.5.0-research.1"
license: Unlicense
repository-code: "https://github.com/llblab/facety"
authors:
  - given-names: "Viacheslav"
    family-names: "Shebuniaev"
abstract: >-
  Facety is a proposed human identification protocol and a Rust simulation
  workbench. It asks how a voluntary network could attach responsibility to
  social guarantees and contest duplicate or fabricated identities without a
  central identity issuer. The design separates FCTY emission from responsibility
  units earned at Self-ID maturity; Integrity adjusts earned units into XP for
  procedural eligibility. The simulator exercises a documented subset, including
  guarantee paths, emission accounting, dispute transitions, and correction
  under trusted premises. Saved results are conditional on modeled behavior and
  historical builds. The evidence-core study concluded REVISE: participation,
  independent recognition accuracy, finite corrective capacity, and real-world
  Sybil resistance remain unverified. This snapshot does not authorize deployment.
keywords:
  - human identification
  - social guarantees
  - distributed responsibility
  - Sybil resistance
  - research simulation
